      "n_units": 644,
      "verification": "Checked by hand on 2026-11-04 against the file, the dataset's mat_files.md and the paper's Methods (Vollan et al. 2025, Nature 639, 995). File: 205,724,904 bytes, the size the EBRAINS bucket lists; its SHA-256 computed from the download. Units: 644, all in units.mec (units.hc is empty), Kilosort labels good 377 and mua 267; the three grid modules hold 48, 90 and 95 units (acorrCluId agrees with each module's unitIds for all 644), with median unit grid scores 1.114, 0.986 and 0.685 and spacings 46, 65 and 93 cm, as the survey loader read them. Time: one listed session, open_field_light_1, 3449 to 5400 s; the 60,000 samples run from 3449.02 to 5047.69 s every 0.01 s, with 173 speed-filter gaps longer than 0.02 s (the longest 253.5 s); 60,000 samples are 600 s, a whole number of 100 s, as the Methods' truncation of awake sessions describes, so the listed session's end is clipped to the recording's, the last spike at 5047.695 s, just after the last sample; the spikes run from 3449.015 s. Space: x from -71.5 to 70.4 cm and y from -70.1 to 70.1 cm, so the unit is metres; the samples' convex hull fills 81% of their minimum rectangle and 94% of their minimum circle, round as the survey found (0.81 and 0.94), so the arena is taken to be the Methods' 150 cm circle; the fitted centre is (-0.5, -1.6) cm and every tracked sample lies inside it. Heading: hd minus the direction of movement above 10 cm/s has a circular mean of +0.2 deg and a median spread of 22.1 deg. Looked at: the overview figure (the path fills the circle; occupancy is sparse, 600 s of speed-filtered samples; heading minus travel is concentrated near 0; the x and y traces jump across the speed-filter gaps, where the raster is blank) and three animation frames: at 25 s the head and its arrow sit where the overview's traces put it, and at 50 s, inside a 7.7 s speed-filter gap, no position is drawn."
    },
